ludes the Dow Jones Industrial  Index and now I'm down to the 30 stocks  this is just me again exploring the data  panthous allows you to explore your data  and I personally like to do that a lot  before I do analysis poke around see  what it looks like so here I'm looking  at the end of the data frame and I see I  have a lot of data there and looking  through the data frame I noticed that  most of the missing data was in the  older dates the shape of the data frame  was 360 by 30 that's 30 years of monthly  data I don't really need that much so I  decided to take the last hundred and  forty-four points the last twelve years  of data  and now I have data beginning in 2007  and there are no missing points at least  as far as I can see there so now the  data this is just me again exploring the  data the shape is 144 two rows I checked  the type of some of the cells to make  sure that the types were converted read  CSV will attempt to convert it to the  proper type but if there's any stray  characters in your CSV file it might  leave everything as strings and there  are methods where you can convert it  manually yourself after cleaning up the  stray characters so let's describe the  data frame data frame has a method  called describe which goes through  column by column and gives you the count  the average and standard deviation min  and Max and the various quartiles of the  data it's another way to look at your  data see what's going on and each of  those attributes also has a method of  its own here I'm calling count and it  gives me back a series which contains  the count for every column and then I  noticed that one of the columns only has  22 five data points I can compare the  series count with the scalar 144 and I  get back a boolean series which tells me  true or false  whether or not the count is less than  144 and now here's the nice thing I can  then take that pooling a series and  filter out the columns that have less  than 144 data points that gives me a  